GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "C031F8C7D1D2BDAC"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{39DF0C519A557AAD}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Mission Overview:"
     m_sContent "Unrest in the country has boiled over. Mujahideen fighters have taken over Kunar Abad by force, sending civilians fleeing from the city. With its close proximity to FOB Michigan, the US Army is left with no choice but to respond in force."\
     ""\
     "Objective:"\
     "US: Clear the city of enemy combatants and blow up any ammo caches"\
     "MUJ: Set up blocking positions while falling back to defend the ammo caches"\
     ""\
     "This Mission does not have any hard end conditions. GM´s discretion (see mission notes)"\
     ""
    }
    GC_Briefing "{2AF68AF6D903B507}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "METREP:"
     m_sContent "<h2>Date:</h2>"\
     "- 2001/08/01"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Light:</h2>"\
     "- First Light: 0645h"\
     "- Last Light: 1715h"\
     "- Time Now: 0700h"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Weather:</h2>"\
     "Clear and sunny with a light haze."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Forecast:</h2>"\
     "Weather is not expected to change"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Moonstate:</h2>"\
     "n/a"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Visibility:</h2>"\
     "Good with light haze around 2000 meters"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{9453956100D4C9EA}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "ENEMY"
     m_sContent "American forces have established a military base to the east of our position. The Americans operate with mechanised infantry, equipped with M16 rifles, machine guns, grenade launchers, and armoured vehicles including M113 APCs and HMMWVs. They have access to substantial ammunition and medical supplies."\
     ""\
     "The Americans wear desert camouflage uniforms and are well-trained soldiers. They will likely conduct a clearing operation through Kunar Abad once they realise we have taken the town. Expect them to move systematically, building by building, and they will not hesitate to use their superior firepower."\
     ""\
     "WARNING: American snipers have been observed in the hills surrounding the city. Many brothers have already been killed trying to move through open ground outside the city limits. DO NOT leave the city - stay within the buildings and streets where their snipers cannot easily target you. The hills are a death trap."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{35613CC8D84AF318}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "I. Situation:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Enemy Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Size, Activity, Location, Unit, Time, and Equipment (SALUTE)</b>"\
     ""\
     "Size: Estimated Company (+) sized element (approx. 50 fighters). Estimate based on multiple transport buses observed entering the AO from the west"\
     ""\
     "Activity: Enemy has seized KUNAR ABAD, established defensive strongpoints, and is currently conducting logistical resupply."\
     ""\
     "Location: Embedded In and around the town."\
     ""\
     "Unit: Mujahideen Fighters / Insurgents."\
     ""\
     "Time: As of 0500. Intelligence is less than 15 minutes old."\
     ""\
     "Equipment: Enemy dressed in standard Afghan civilian clothing; armed with Bolt Action rifles, AK-pattern rifles, machine guns, and limited anti-tank rocket launchers."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Capabilities and Limitations (DRAW-DG)</b>"\
     ""\
     "Defend: YES. Enemy is dug in urban terrain. They will likely use buildings and civilians for cover."\
     ""\
     "Reinforce: POSSIBLE. If the buses left, they may return with more fighters, though current assessment is that the main force is already inside."\
     ""\
     "Attack: YES. Their goal is to stage an attack from this city. They have the capability to launch local counter-attacks against our entry."\
     ""\
     "Withdraw: UNLIKELY. Enemy appears determined to hold the logistics hub."\
     ""\
     "Delay: YES. May use snipers or skirmishers on outskirts to slow our advance"\
     ""\
     "Gas: NONE OBSERVED."\
     ""\
     "<b>3. Enemy’s Most Likely and Most Dangerous Courses of Action</b>"\
     ""\
     "Most Likely Course of Action (MLCOA): Enemy will retreat when met with overwhelming force"\
     ""\
     "Most Dangerous Course of Action (MDCOA): Enemy will stronghold buildings and fight to the last element"\
     ""\
     "<h2>B. Friendly Forces</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Higher’s Mission & Intent</b>"\
     ""\
     "Mission: "\
     "1st Battalion CLEARS the KUNAR Valley IOT deny enemy staging grounds and restore freedom of movement to the region."\
     ""\
     "Intent: "\
     "Purpose: Secure the population and disrupt enemy offensive capabilities."\
     "Endstate: All towns in sector cleared of insurgent forces; MSRs safe for civilian traffic."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Adjacent Units</b>"\
     "North: Bravo Company (1st Platoon) - Establishing Blocking Position grid 028-022 (AI)"\
     "South: Bravo Company (2nd Platoon) - Establishing Blocking Position grid 035-030 (AI)"\
     "West: None (Open terrain / Enemy territory)."\
     "East: FOB Michigan (Rear Area)."\
     ""\
     "<b>3. Supporting</b>"\
     "Recon Element: Currently in observation post (OP) overlooking KUNAR ABAD. Providing real-time intelligence. (AI)"\
     ""\
     "Fires: None assigned. (Restrictive ROE due to civilians)."\
     ""\
     "<h2>C. Attachments/Detachment</h2>"\
     "<b>Attachments</b>"\
     "2x M1151A1 with Gunner/Driver attached to Company"\
     "1x HMG section attached to each Platoon"\
     ""\
     "<b>Detachments: 3rd Platoon.</b>"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{EC4A557B46274608}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "FRIENDLY FORCES"
     m_sContent "The Amir with Red and Green leader is our main force. More brothers are expected to arrive in the evening, but for now our roughly 40 men is all we got to defend Kunar Abad."\
     ""\
     "Our transport buses that brought us from Asadabad and the Shuryak Valley have been positioned as roadblocks on the western approaches to deny the Americans easy entry with their vehicles."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{6B703A542E96365B}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "II. Mission:"
     m_sContent "NLT 0500, Alpha Company CLEARS KUNAR ABAD, DESTROYS enemy caches, and ESTABLISHES Blocking Position to the West IOT DISRUPT enemy offensive operations."\
     ""\
     "Endstate: Cache destroyed and blocking position established in the Police Station (034-025) and Mosque (033-027)"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{DA71C2E5BEAC638A}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "MISSION"
     m_sContent "The Amir has ordered that we defend Kunar Abad and the ammunition cache for as long as possible. "\
     "This city is critical as we are establishing a staging point for our planned assault on the American base. Every hour we hold this ground gives our commanders time to prepare the offensive."\
     ""\
     "Task Priority"\
     "1. Stay alive"\
     "2. Delay american fighters from moving through the city"\
     "3. Hold the compound with the ammunition cache (0324-0261) for as long as possibile."\
     "4. Fall back to the Mosque (033-027) and Police Station (034-025) and fight to the last man."\
     ""\
     "[Green line at the front is your AO limit. Notice how the hills to the south and north is outside of your AO]"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{ED2263A907CD590C}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "III. Execution:"
     m_sContent "As per Company Brief"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{6E4AEAA74A655356}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "TASKS AND ORDERS"
     m_sContent "The defence of Kunar Abad is lead by the Amir who will command his two leaders:"\
     "Red Leader (Located in the city near the market)"\
     "- Red 1, Red 2, Red 3"\
     "Green Leader (Located near the Mosque, north of the river)"\
     "- Green 1, Green 2, Green 3"\
     ""\
     "Your responsibilities:"\
     "a) Defend Kunar Abad - STAY WITHIN THE CITY LIMITS"\
     "b) Maintain observation on American movements and report via the radioman"\
     "c) Coordinate with other fighter groups in the city when possible"\
     "d) Use the urban terrain to your advantage - buildings provide cover and ambush positions"\
     "e) Preserve fighter strength - withdraw and reposition when faced with overwhelming force rather than dying needlessly"\
     "f) DO NOT attempt to move into the hills - American snipers will kill you"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CBD1C70ABAB611B4}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "IV. Sustainment:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Administration</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Enemy Prisoners of War (EPW):</b>"\
     ""\
     "Handling: Adhere to the 5 S's (Search, Silence, Segregate, Speed, Safeguard)."\
     "Collection: Any surrendered enemies are to be zip-tied and moved to the Company HQ location immediately. Do not leave them with the assaulting sections."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Casualty Evacuation:</b>"\
     "Self-aid immediately, drag serious wounds to Platoon HQ for the medic, and consolidate everyone at Company HQ once secure—we do not evacuate."\
     ""\
     "<h2>B. Logistics</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Supply (Beans, Bullets, & Batteries):</b>"\
     ""\
     "All personnel are issued a standard combat load and Individual IFAK."\
     ""\
     "Additional ammunition, smoke grenades, demolition blocks and medical supplies are available from vehicles."\
     ""\
     "Only medics may draw extra morphine injectors, saline solutions, epinephrine, and ammonium carbonate."\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Transportation & Maintenance:</b>"\
     "2x M1151A1 (seats 5)"\
     "1x Ambulance (seats 3 + 2 beds)"\
     "1x M998 (seats 4)"\
     ""\
     ""\
     "<b>3. Communications & Pyrotechnics:</b>"\
     ""\
     "All units will maintain radio contact with higher headquarters and internal elements."\
     ""\
     "Signal flares and other pyrotechnics are issued as per SOP."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{4A60877A37515B57}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "SUPPORT"\
     ""
     m_sContent "Red Leader have acces to 3 motorbikes (each seats 2)"\
     "Green Leader have access to two transport Urals (each seats 15)"\
     "The buses cannot move from their blocking positions. No artillery or air support is available."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{7786F1023068D921}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "V. Command & Control:"
     m_sContent "<h2>A. Signal</h2>"\
     "<b>1. Radios:</b>"\
     ""\
     "All Squad Leaders (SL), Platoon Sergeants (PSG), Platoon Leaders (PL), Company Commander (CO) and the Company XO are equipped with AN/PRC-68 radios. Signalers are equipped with AN/PRC-77"\
     ""\
     "<b>2. Radio Nets</b>"\
     ""\
     "/// PRR Nets:"\
     "Reference ingame “Group Menu” default keybind “P”"\
     ""\
     "/// LRR Net:"\
     "48.00Mhz - Company Net"\
     "47.00Mhz - 1st Platoon Net"\
     "49.00Mhz - 2nd Platoon Net"\
     ""\
     "<b>4. Recognition Signals</b>"\
     ""\
     "Green Smoke: Location of friendly forces"\
     ""\
     "Red Smoke: Location of enemy forces"\
     ""\
     "Yellow Smoke: Wounded or requesting aid"\
     ""\
     "White Smoke: Concealment"\
     ""\
     "<b>5. Challenge and Password</b>"\
     ""\
     "Challenge: CO SHOULD WRITE ON MAP"\
     ""\
     "Password: CO SHOULD WRITE ON MAP"\
     ""\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{3909F8759C11329C}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "COMMAND AND SIGNALS"
     m_sContent "Only the radiomen carries a radio (R-148). All communication with lower sections must be through runners or face-to-face contact. Conserve radio batteries - only critical information should be transmitted."\
     ""\
     "Radio Net: 50.00MHz - Main Command Net"\
     ""\
     "<b>Command</b>"\
     "Overall command for the defence of Kunar Abad rests with the Amir. Section leaders will direct local tactics in your assigned sectors."\
     ""\
     "Chain of command:"\
     "- Amir"\
     "- Red Leader"\
     "- Green Leader"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{9C963ECAB29656C0}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "WEATHER"
     m_sContent "Date: 2001/08/01"\
     "Time Now: 0700h (first light)"\
     "Weather: Clear and sunny with light haze"\
     "Visibility: Good, approximately 2000 metres"\
     "Temperature: Hot - conserve water"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CED57640DEA2AF3C}" {
     m_iOrder 14
     m_sTitle "FINAL GUIDANCE"
     m_sContent "Brothers, we fight for our land and our future. The Americans have superior equipment and training, but we have determination and knowledge of this ground. Use the buildings, use the narrow streets, make them pay for every metre. When they come in strength, fall back and regroup - live to fight again."\
     ""\
     "REMEMBER: Stay in the city. The hills belong to their snipers. Many good fighters have died learning this lesson - do not be the next."\
     ""\
     "Allah is with us. Fight with courage and cunning."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{161227E18061F6F4}" {
     m_iOrder 15
     m_sTitle "VI. Mission notes:"
     m_sContent "<h2>Mission Intent</h2>"\
     "US: Conduct a Cordon and Search operation in Kunar Abad. Clear all structures and destroy any localized Ammo Caches. Once complete, establish a blocking position towards Shan Kalay."\
     ""\
     "MUJ: Conduct asymmetric defense. Delay the US advance, inflict maximum casualties, and prevent the US from securing the sector within the time limit."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Trench building</h2>"\
     "Trench building: Disabled."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Setup timer</h2>"\
     "US: 5 Minutes"\
     "MUJ: None"\
     ""\
     "<h2>JIP Teleport</h2>"\
     "Disabled"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Endconditions</h2>"\
     "<b>BLUFOR (US) Victory Criteria:</b>"\
     "- Major Victory: Ammo cache destroyed AND Company established in blocking position at Shan Kalay (Grids 034025 / 033027)."\
     ""\
     "- Minor Victory: Company established in blocking position at Shan Kalay (Grids 034025 / 033027), but failed to locate/destroy the Ammo cache."\
     ""\
     "- Pyrrhic Victory: Achieved either condition above, but sustained 60%+ casualties."\
     ""\
     "<b>OPFOR (MUJ) Victory Criteria:</b>"\
     "- Major Victory: Inflict 90% casualties on US forces, OR prevent US forces from reaching the blocking position before the time limit (70 min)."\
     ""\
     "- Pyrrhic Victory: Achieved Major Victory conditions, but sustained 60%+ casualties."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Timelimit of 70 min</h2>"\
     ""\
     "Automated messages will trigger for Time Limits (70 min), Casualty Thresholds (60% / 90%) and if the ammo cache is destroyed. GMs is expected to call when Blocking Positions are reached."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Mission by Perfk</h2>"\
     "Last updated: 2026-02-12"\
     ""
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
